# Day 5 Mini Project: Login Page Automation

## Objective
Automate login to the Herokuapp demo application using Java and
Selenium WebDriver, validate successful login, and capture screenshots.

## Tools Used
- Java
- Selenium WebDriver
- Google Chrome
- ChromeDriver

## Test Website
https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/login

## Test Credentials
- Username: tomsmith
- Password: SuperSecretPassword!

## Test Steps
1. Launch Chrome and maximize the browser window.
2. Open the login page.
3. Wait for the username field to become visible.
4. Enter the username and password.
5. Capture a screenshot of the completed login form.
6. Click the Login button.
7. Wait for navigation to the secure area.
8. Verify that the message contains:
   "You logged into a secure area!"
9. Capture a screenshot of the login result.
10. Close the browser.

## Expected Result
The user reaches the secure area and sees the success message.
The console displays "PASS: Login successful".

## Screenshot Handling
Screenshots are saved in the screenshots folder:
- login_form_filled.png
- login_result.png
- login_failure.png — captured if the test fails

## Synchronization
Explicit waits allow up to 10 seconds for required elements
or navigation, reducing failures caused by page-loading delays.

## Failure Handling
Unexpected login results cause an AssertionError.
Test failures trigger a screenshot attempt before the error is rethrown.
The browser closes through the finally block.

## Assumptions
- Java, Chrome, and Selenium are configured.
- The test website is reachable.
- Demo credentials and element locators remain unchanged.
- The project has permission to create screenshot files.

## Scope
This project validates successful login only.
Registration, invalid login, and logout are outside its scope.